---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import socialPost from "../../assets/work/noz/noz-social-post.png";

const tags = ["Social Media", "Content Design", "Canva", "Instagram", "Brand Voice"];

const pillars = ["Retail and shopping moments", "Lifestyle and user-generated content", "SPF education"];
---

<Base
  title="Nöz: Designing an Instagram Post | Grace Joy Park"
  description="Grace Joy Park's social media case study: designing an Instagram post in Canva and building the brand voice for Nöz, a simulated SPF brand, through the Global Career Accelerator."
>
  <p class="back"><a href="/work">&larr; Back to Work</a></p>

  <article class="post">
    <h1>Nöz: Designing an Instagram Post</h1>
    <p class="meta muted">The Global Career Accelerator &middot; June 2026 &middot; Social Media</p>

    <ul class="tags">
      {tags.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
    </ul>

    <figure class="design-figure">
      <Image
        src={socialPost}
        alt="Instagram post for Nöz showing four neon SPF sticks with the headline SPF that goes where you do"
        widths={[400, 700, 1080]}
        sizes="(max-width: 720px) 85vw, 440px"
        format="webp"
      />
      <figcaption>The Instagram post I designed for Nöz in Canva. (Design/Grace Park)</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        I designed an Instagram post for Nöz and built the social strategy around it, from
        competitor research to the brand voice I used to answer comments. Nöz is a simulated
        brand the Global Career Accelerator provides for training, so this was a project
        build rather than a real account.
      </p>

      <h2>The post</h2>
      <p>
        I designed the post in Canva for the product photography pillar. I lined up the four
        neon Nöz sticks on a soft gradient so the colors do most of the selling, then kept
        the copy short. &ldquo;SPF that goes where you do&rdquo; leads, and a single line
        underneath, &ldquo;Colorful, reef-safe sun care for every day outside,&rdquo;
        explains the product. I wanted a post that reads as a style brand first and a
        sunscreen second, which is how Nöz wants to show up.
      </p>

      <h2>Competitor research</h2>
      <p>
        Before designing, I studied @supergoop, a Nöz competitor, and pulled three content
        pillars from its feed:
      </p>
      <ul class="pillars">
        {pillars.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p>
        I compared its Instagram and TikTok and found the same themes on both, just more
        casual and video-first on TikTok. That gave me a map for where my post fit and what
        the product photography pillar needed to look like to feel at home in the feed.
      </p>

      <h2>Brand voice</h2>
      <p>
        The project also covered community management. I drafted Nöz replies to comments
        across TikTok, Instagram, Reddit, X, Facebook and Pinterest, following an escalation
        plan that decides when a brand should respond. I kept the voice warm and consistent
        while still handling pricing pushback and product complaints. One reply I wrote to a
        comment comparing prices:
      </p>
      <blockquote class="reply">
        We love that you&rsquo;re excited to take Nöz with you. For anyone comparing prices,
        our SPF 45 sticks are made with reef-safe, vegan ingredients and biodegradable
        cardboard packaging, so you&rsquo;re getting sun care that works hard and treats the
        planet kindly.
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <section class="why-section">
      <h2>What I Learned</h2>
      <p>
        Designing the post taught me to let the product colors carry the message and to
        write copy that fits a feed instead of an essay. Writing the replies taught me how a
        brand holds one voice across very different platforms and audiences, even when the
        comment is a complaint.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .back { margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }

  .post h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tags {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .tags li {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .design-figure {
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    max-width: 440px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .design-figure :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .design-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .prose p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .prose .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .pillars {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .pillars li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .reply {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .why-section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .why-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .why-section p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
